<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Cypress Semiconductor cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Cypress Semiconductor cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Rodman &amp; Renshaw Inc said Tuesday it downgraded Cypress Semiconductor Corp to neutral from a buy rating, and also lowered its earnings estimates for 1997 to $0.50 a share from $0.70 and for 1998 to $1.00 from $1.30.</p>
<p>-- In a report, Rodman said a possible flow in a new Intel Corp microprocessor could delay an expected increase demand for SRAMs, which are memory parts used in personal computers, which Cypress manufactures.</p>
<p>-- Cypress shares were off 3/8 at 14-5/8.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
